      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranier%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "From the 1910s to the 1920s, Ranier earned the nickname “Port of Rainy Lake” amid a boom of hotels, saloons, and sawmills.",
